  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Count the groups of nodes in an undirected graph. Two nodes belong to one group if a sequence of edges connects them; an isolated node is a group by itself.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 5, edges = [[0,1],[1,2],[3,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2</pre>\n  <p>The first three nodes form one group and the last two another.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 4, edges = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre>\n  <p>Each isolated node is its own component.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 0, edges = []\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>An empty graph has zero components.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= n &lt;= 100</code>; nodes have IDs <code>0</code> through <code>n-1</code>.</li>\n    <li>Each edge has two distinct valid endpoints; no edge is repeated.</li>\n    <li>There are at most <code>1000</code> edges.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
